1. Definitions

"Program" means the Project Desktop program: its source code,
documentation, builds (executables), and any changes or additions to them.

"Licensor" means the owner of the GitHub account LORD07Sson, who holds the
copyright in the Program and administers the Project team. The Licensor may
be identified in more detail by a written notice added to this repository.

"Team" means the group of people the Licensor works with on the Project
project.

"Member" means a person whose membership in the Team has been confirmed by
the Licensor under section 4 and has not ended.

2. Permission

For as long as a person is a Member, the Licensor grants that person a
non-transferable, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable permission to:

a) run and use the Program for work on the Project project;
b) read the Program's source code and modify it solely for the needs of
   the Project project.

3. Restrictions

No one, including a Member, may:

a) distribute the Program, its source code or builds, publish them, give
   them to anyone who is not a Member, or make them publicly available;
b) sublicense the Program or transfer rights in it;
c) use the Program or parts of it in other products or projects, or for the
   benefit of third parties;
d) remove or alter copyright notices or this license.

Hosting. If the Licensor keeps a copy of the Program on a hosting platform
such as GitHub, that does not grant anyone any right beyond this license.
The only exception is the rights that the platform's own terms of service
give to other users of that platform (for example, viewing the repository
and forking it within the platform). Those rights do not include running,
modifying, or distributing the Program, or using it for any other purpose.

4. Membership and termination

Who is a Member. A person becomes a Member when the Licensor confirms their
membership in the Team in writing (a message in the Team's usual channel, an
email, or an entry in a roster of Members kept by the Licensor). The
Licensor decides in good faith who is a Member. Absent manifest error, the
Licensor's roster and messages are conclusive evidence of membership.

When membership ends. A person stops being a Member on the earliest of:

a) the date stated in a written notice from the Licensor to that person
   (sent by any channel the Licensor has used to contact them), or, if no
   date is stated, the moment the notice is sent;
b) the moment the person tells the Licensor in writing that they are
   leaving the Team;
c) 90 days without any participation in the project, unless the Licensor
   confirms in writing that the person remains a Member.

Effect. The permission in section 2 ends automatically for a person when
they stop being a Member, and for anyone who breaches any term of this
license. After that, the former Member may not use, modify, or distribute
the Program or parts of it under this license, and must stop using them and
delete all copies of the source code and builds in their possession within
14 days.

5. Copyright and contributions

Copyright in the Program remains with the Licensor. This license grants no
rights other than those expressly stated in section 2. Anyone who
contributes changes or additions to the Program for the Project project
(a "contributor") grants the Licensor all rights needed to include those
changes in the Program and license them under this license; the changes
become part of the Program unless the Licensor and the contributor agree
otherwise in writing. Nothing in this license transfers rights in code that
a contributor did not create or has no right to license.

6. Third-party components

The Program may use third-party libraries and tools (for example ffmpeg,
mpv and others). They remain under their own licenses; this license does
not apply to them and does not override their terms.

